From 0218cded6ca43e912c9917397b9cef7a2de622b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Zaritskyi <viktorzarickiy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 21:46:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] input: himax_hx83112b - add SPI transport and hx83102e
 support

The hx83102e is the same touch controller family but is attached over
SPI rather than I2C, and it speaks a framed protocol: a one-byte command
(0xf2 write, 0xf3 read) followed by a three-byte header on reads. Add a
regmap_bus implementation for it and split the driver's probe into a
transport-independent core with I2C and SPI front ends.

The part also needs its event stack drained after reset, and it holds
its reset line low longer than the other members of the family, so
describe both per-chip: post_reset_delay_us and event_stack_size.

Signed-off-by: Viktor Zaritskyi <viktorzarickiy@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
